WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.960
Most cortical interneurons are born in another region, the ventral forebrain.

2
00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:10.820
So how could a cortical organoid get them?

3
00:00:11.733 --> 00:00:12.893
Supply the region.

4
00:00:13.813 --> 00:00:18.513
In 2017, Sergiu Pașca's group at Stanford grew the two regions separately.

5
00:00:18.513 --> 00:00:19.513
In 2017, Sergio Pashka's group at Stanford grew the two regions separately.

6
00:00:19.717 --> 00:00:23.757
They labelled the ventral cells, then let one spheroid of each kind fuse.

7
00:00:24.817 --> 00:00:28.177
Predict. Which way will the labelled cells move?

8
00:00:29.157 --> 00:00:30.157
And how?

9
00:00:36.017 --> 00:00:40.537
They moved from the ventral partner into the cortical one, far more often than the

10
00:00:40.537 --> 00:00:41.537
reverse.

11
00:00:41.917 --> 00:00:43.177
They moved in jumps.

12
00:00:44.037 --> 00:00:45.237
A leading process extends.

13
00:00:46.197 --> 00:00:48.057
A swelling forms ahead of the nucleus.

14
00:00:48.997 --> 00:00:50.037
Then the nucleus follows.

15
00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:53.477
Fetal interneurons move the same way.

16
00:00:54.177 --> 00:00:57.837
Once inside, the cells received excitatory synaptic input.

17
00:01:01.767 --> 00:01:07.047
Then came cells from people with Timothy syndrome, caused by a mutation in a calcium

18
00:01:07.047 --> 00:01:08.047
channel gene.

19
00:01:08.817 --> 00:01:11.937
Patient interneurons made more jumps, but shorter ones.

20
00:01:12.857 --> 00:01:14.577
Overall, they moved less efficiently.

21
00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:19.800
Fused to control cortex, patient interneurons still showed the defect.

22
00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:23.180
So it lay at least partly in the interneurons themselves.

23
00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:27.260
Blocking L-type calcium channels improved their migration.

24
00:01:28.383 --> 00:01:33.343
Those two experiments, not the channel's location, point to a defect in the cells'

25
00:01:33.343 --> 00:01:36.163
own program. An assembloid can show it.

26
00:01:37.033 --> 00:01:38.533
A host restores more.

27
00:01:39.433 --> 00:01:42.733
Human organoids were transplanted into newborn rat cortex.

28
00:01:43.693 --> 00:01:48.213
As the rats matured, the grafts gained a blood supply and responded to whisker

29
00:01:48.213 --> 00:01:49.213
deflection.

30
00:01:52.067 --> 00:01:58.067
In 2013, Lancaster and colleagues grew organoids from a person with microcephaly, a

31
00:01:58.067 --> 00:01:59.767
brain far smaller than normal.

32
00:02:00.647 --> 00:02:04.927
The patient carried mutations in a gene called CDK5RAP2.

33
00:02:05.667 --> 00:02:08.627
The patient's organoids had smaller progenitor zones.

34
00:02:09.467 --> 00:02:10.767
Is the mutation to blame?

35
00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:16.820
Predict. Name three other explanations, and a control that tests each.

36
00:02:23.233 --> 00:02:24.973
The rest of that person's genes.

37
00:02:25.993 --> 00:02:29.633
Several donors help, but only moving the gene itself really tests this.

38
00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:32.163
A quirk of one cell line.

39
00:02:33.083 --> 00:02:34.883
Several clones from the patient test that.

40
00:02:35.833 --> 00:02:40.693
A bad batch. Grow patient and control side by side, more than once.

41
00:02:41.617 --> 00:02:43.937
These controls strengthen the comparison.

42
00:02:44.777 --> 00:02:46.077
Then move the gene itself.

43
00:02:46.917 --> 00:02:52.837
Put back into patient tissue, CDK5RAP2 kept more cells as radial glia.

44
00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:59.080
Reduced in control tissue by two different hairpin RNAs, it let cells shift toward

45
00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:00.080
neurons.

46
00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:04.820
Why was the organoid a good bet?

47
00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:09.460
The protein works at the centrosome, inside the dividing progenitor.

48
00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:13.940
The rescue and knockdown, done in organoid tissue, made it a result.

49
00:03:14.983 --> 00:03:19.903
If a gene acted through blood vessels or microglia, a normal-looking organoid would

50
00:03:19.903 --> 00:03:20.903
not clear it.

51
00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:23.587
Use the program to choose where to start.

52
00:03:24.347 --> 00:03:28.587
Then test the organoid, hardest where the surroundings matter, and measure every

53
00:03:28.587 --> 00:03:31.327
feature, because the dish adds stress of its own.
